{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790432064,"nonce":"XymviTRTEvcg2apaUgOmcRC9KNk=","message":"Resolved with wren-lift-dc (2026-09-26, WrenLift bed5dd5): the aot_runtime object defines no _start, main or __main_void (checked with llvm-nm), so it adds no entry. The bootstrap is in WrenLift's program object. Its LLVM AOT will get an entry option: Main (the default, standalone) emits __main_void/main; Library emits the bootstrap as an exported wlift_program_run(vm: *mut WrenVM) -\u003e i32 (0, or 70 on an uncaught error). That fills the program's tables, installs its classes and closures and runs the module bodies. It creates no VM and frees none, so caribou-wren calls it with the VM it made on caribou's heap. It would be namespaced per program if a link ever holds several. They land it when this issue needs it. Also needed from the Library object: caribou::link's per-member C-ABI thunks, which Haxe's object calls directly, must be exported too, not internal.","files":null}]}